# UDB docker compose deployment — environment
#
# Do not edit secrets in by hand. Run:
#
#   ./scripts/init.sh
#
# It copies this file to .env, replaces the Postgres password placeholder, and
# runs `udb env fill` inside the broker image, which appends the generated
# secrets (marked "Added by `udb env fill`") and writes the RS256 key pair to
# ./secrets. A value already set in .env is never changed.
#
# This file is read twice: by docker compose for ${...} in docker-compose.yml,
# and by the broker container (env_file). Keep it LF, one KEY=value per line, no
# quotes. The full variable reference is the repo's top-level .env.example.

# ── Image ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Broker image and pinned release. Change the version deliberately; never `latest`.
UDB_IMAGE=ghcr.io/fahara02/udb
UDB_VERSION=0.6.15

# ── Postgres (the one mandatory backend) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Password of the `udb` role in the bundled Postgres. init.sh replaces the
# placeholder here AND in UDB_PG_DSN with one random value. It only takes effect
# the first time the volume is created.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me-pg-password
# Direct (session) endpoint the broker and the udb CLI use. Not a transaction pooler.
UDB_PG_DSN=postgres://udb:change-me-pg-password@postgres:5432/udb?sslmode=disable

# ── Posture ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# development = TLS terminated outside the broker (nginx, a mesh, or a private
# network). `production` forces broker TLS + mandatory mTLS; see README
# "Switching to production" before changing it.
UDB_ENV=development
# Identifies this broker in logs, metrics and audit records.
UDB_APP_NAME=udb
# Log filter for the broker (tracing env-filter syntax).
RUST_LOG=info

# ── Listeners (inside the container) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Data plane (DataBroker). The compose command passes the same address.
UDB_GRPC_ADDR=0.0.0.0:50051
# The native control plane (auth, authz and the other udb.core.* services) is
# set in docker-compose.yml (UDB_AUTH_GRPC_ADDR=0.0.0.0:50061): its address is
# part of the container layout, not a per-site choice.

# ── Authentication ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Server-side sessions; without them login returns FAILED_PRECONDITION.
UDB_SESSION_ENABLED=true
# Generated by init.sh (`udb env fill`), do not set by hand here:
#   UDB_SESSION_HASH_SECRET   hashes session tokens (and passwords, as a fallback)
#   UDB_API_KEY_HASH_SECRET   hashes API keys
#   UDB_PASSWORD_HASH_SECRET  hashes native user passwords (init.sh adds it)
#   UDB_ENCRYPTION_KEY        at-rest key for secret columns and vault material; LOSING IT LOSES THAT DATA
#   UDB_APPROVAL_SIGNING_KEY  signs migration approval plans
#   UDB_JWT_PRIVATE_KEY       /run/udb-secrets/jwt-private.pem, signs the broker's bearer tokens
#   UDB_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY        /run/udb-secrets/jwt-public.pem, verifies them

# ── Transport ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Broker-side TLS and client certificates. Off here: put a TLS proxy in front
# (examples/docker_nginx) or switch to production (README).
UDB_TLS_REQUIRED=false
UDB_MTLS_REQUIRED=false

# ── Schema ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Apply schema changes from the served protos on startup. For production set
# false and apply reviewed plans with `udb plan` (README).
UDB_MIGRATE_ENABLED=true

# ── Optional backends ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Boot even when an optional backend (Redis, object store, Kafka, ...) is not
# configured: the native services that need it answer FAILED_PRECONDITION
# instead of the broker refusing to start. Set false once every backend your
# services use is configured, so a missing one stops the boot loudly.
UDB_ALLOW_DEGRADED_BACKENDS=true
# Deliver UDB's events through the durable Postgres journal, without Kafka.
# Set false when you enable Kafka (README "Turn on Kafka").
UDB_CDC_JOURNAL_ONLY=true

# ── Object storage (only when the MinIO block is enabled) ────────────────────
# Root credentials of the bundled MinIO; the broker gets the same pair.
# MINIO_ROOT_USER=udb
# MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=change-me-minio-password

# ── LiveKit (only when the LiveKit block is enabled) ─────────────────────────
# API key/secret pair LiveKit and the broker share. `--dev` LiveKit uses devkey/secret.
# LIVEKIT_API_KEY=devkey
# LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=secret

# ── Host port bindings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Interface the published ports bind to. Loopback by default: put a TLS proxy
# in front instead of exposing the broker. 0.0.0.0 exposes them on every interface.
UDB_BIND=127.0.0.1
